 ## Key Design Decisions
 
 - **Commands over HTTPS, one authoritative board per event.** Editors submit commands to the server, which assigns each committed edit one event revision. Peer-to-peer or browser-side merging was rejected: the tenets require one authoritative revision regardless of delivery route, and offline editing is a non-goal.
+
+- **Self-hosted WebSockets for change delivery.** Chosen over five-second HTTPS polling and hosted realtime services. Accepts connection management and reconnect complexity to avoid recurring vendor fees and provider coupling. The change store must support replayable revisions; delivery owns session lifecycle and replay; browser sync implements reconnect with catch-up. See [Decision: Change Delivery Approach](docs/decisions/change-delivery-approach.md).
